From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:42:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: attach the per-tab helpers Chromium 157
 moved to TabFeatures

Chromium 157 moved most per-tab helpers out of TabHelpers::AttachTabHelpers()
into tabs::TabFeatures (Init() and WillDiscardContents()). TabFeatures needs a
TabInterface in a Browser; Open Arc's tabs have neither, so after the upgrade
they lost the favicon driver, history, the password manager client, the
subresource filter (which the ad blocker forces on), translate, page-specific
content settings, PermissionRequestManager, the popup blocker, installable
manager, top sites, site engagement, page-load metrics, HTTPS-only mode and
more. Favicons, most-visited pages and the password dropdown stopped working.

TabHelpersAccess::AttachTabHelpers() now creates the WebContents-scoped helpers
itself, in TabFeatures::WillDiscardContents() order and with its conditions
(platform autofill, off-the-record, feature flags, build flags). The helpers
TabFeatures keeps as plain members are owned by a WebContentsUserData that
lives as long as the WebContents. That holder also owns
ManagePasswordsUIController through the embedder constructor of patch 0023
(registered in the holder's UnownedUserDataHost, found through
SetEmbedderUserDataHostLookup(), destroyed in WebContentsDestroyed()), so the
password save/update prompt works again. NetErrorTabHelper is owned the
same way, through the embedder constructor of patch "let an embedder own a
tab's NetErrorTabHelper", so error pages get their final DNS probe status
(probes stay off, plan C27). Other helpers that need a TabInterface
(TabDialogs, CoreTabHelper, PopupOpenerTabHelper, ...) are skipped; the list
is in the code.

Needed by plan tasks C6b, C9, C13, C16, C36 and B123 on Chromium 157. Upstream
behaviour without it: a WebContents outside a Browser tab strip gets only
session, zoom, infobar and autofill helpers.
